Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.93,0:00:02.97,Default,James,0,0,0,,I'm so relieved.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.97,0:00:08.63,Default,James,0,0,0,,Your spirit isn't broken. You've only \Ncautiously locked yourself away.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.63,0:00:10.23,Default,James,0,0,0,,Am I wrong,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:10.46,0:00:12.39,Default,James,0,0,0,,Pamela Francis?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.92,0:00:16.72,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,Don't you want revenge?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.75,0:00:23.49,Default,Krishna,0,0,0,,Revenge on the one who did this \Nto you: Constance Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.00,0:00:30.33,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Constance Grail!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.48,0:02:06.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship, how is Kimberly?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.22,0:02:08.35,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Safe.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:08.35,0:02:12.14,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Her arm was injured, but she should \Nbe out of the hospital soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.14,0:02:13.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:14.70,0:02:21.11,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That ledger allowed us to arrest Simon \NDarkian for falsifying official documents.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.79,0:02:25.75,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,His wife, Deborah, has been sent \Nto the Rudolph Convent
Dialogue: 0,0:02:25.75,0:02:30.18,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,on suspicion of human trafficking \Nand smuggling Jackal's Paradise.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:30.63,0:02:35.65,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,This ought to strip Daeg Gallus \Nof its biggest backer.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.19,0:02:42.64,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,How are you fine ladies today?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.64,0:02:44.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Lucia!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:44.27,0:02:45.65,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,You're going out?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.65,0:02:51.40,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Yes! I'm going to buy sweets for Abby,\Nsince she's been so busy!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.75,0:02:54.07,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Now, if you'll excuse me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:55.66,0:02:59.52,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,I can't believe the Darkians \Nwere a party to smuggling.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.18,0:03:02.71,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Debby didn't used to be like that.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.32,0:03:09.51,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,So, did Simon know where \Nto find Prince Ulysses?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:09.91,0:03:15.65,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,No, and we have mere days \Nbefore the Farisian delegation departs.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.11,0:03:18.66,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,If we don't locate \Nthe prince before then...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:19.04,0:03:21.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,It will mean war?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.56,0:03:28.90,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Do any Daeg Gallus collaborators \Ncontrol a harbor?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.90,0:03:29.96,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Why a harbor?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:31.46,0:03:36.86,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,The kidnapper is a merchant with \Nan unusual skin tone by our standards,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:36.86,0:03:39.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,yet not a soul has reported seeing him.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.37,0:03:46.40,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,So, suppose the prince is someplace \Na man like that wouldn't stand out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.33,0:03:49.58,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That's her idea. Does it help?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.58,0:03:52.39,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Of course! Kiara Grafton.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:52.97,0:03:55.07,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,There's a wharf on her family's lands.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:55.56,0:03:57.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh! With the Daeg Gallus tattoo!
Dialogue: 0,0:03:58.47,0:04:01.94,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,She must have warehouses \Nperfect for hiding a person.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.61,0:04:03.92,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'll go investigate.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.47,0:04:06.83,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I... I'll go with you!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.54,0:04:11.51,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Abby!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:12.82,0:04:15.10,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Thank goodness. You're all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:15.10,0:04:16.31,Default,Abigail,0,0,0,,Why wouldn't I be?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.78,0:04:18.44,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,I got a tip.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.44,0:04:22.06,Default,Aldous,0,0,0,,Deborah Darkian has escaped\N from the convent.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.56,0:04:30.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,A-Are you angry that \NI insisted on coming?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.52,0:04:34.70,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,No. I was reminding myself
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.70,0:04:39.56,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,that it's better to keep you in my sights\Nthan to let you run off on your own.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.97,0:04:41.96,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,He has a point.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:44.38,0:04:45.46,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That said,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.04,0:04:49.92,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I may not need to keep an eye\N on you much longer.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:51.59,0:04:56.02,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,When we locate Prince Ulysses \Nand all of this is resolved,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.02,0:04:58.42,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,the two of you will have\N achieved your goal too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.68,0:05:00.73,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.99,0:05:03.48,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,I don't want to hear this.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:04.00,0:05:09.64,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,So I'll arrange things for you to dissolve\Nour engagement when the time comes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:10.07,0:05:12.74,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Such that no blame falls \Non you, of course.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:15.37,0:05:17.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What about Your Lordship?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.52,0:05:24.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Won't you marry?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.19,0:05:32.61,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,No. I have no faith that \NI could make a wife happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:38.57,0:05:40.33,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What a silly man.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:43.52,0:05:46.19,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,You certainly bought a lot, Lady Lucia.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.19,0:05:50.03,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Indeed! I just know Abby will love these!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.53,0:05:52.73,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,Come now!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.28,0:05:55.25,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,I'll retrieve it at once!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.54,0:06:08.20,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,I know you.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.67,0:06:11.58,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Raise your voice and I'll slit her throat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.58,0:06:13.91,Default,Maidservant A,0,0,0,,L-Lady Lucia...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.80,0:06:19.04,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Kindly release that woman, Lady Deborah.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.04,0:06:21.05,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,It's me you're after, is it not?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.39,0:06:29.07,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,So, this is the warehouse.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.60,0:06:31.63,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,It's awfully quiet.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:32.38,0:06:34.21,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I'll take a peek inside.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.36,0:06:37.72,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.72,0:06:39.37,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, right.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:49.26,0:06:50.36,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Run!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.26,0:06:59.26,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:59.26,0:07:00.74,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:00.74,0:07:01.95,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.49,0:07:07.91,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Where are they firing from?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:07.91,0:07:09.23,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Over there!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.23,0:07:11.23,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,She says there's one on that roof!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.02,0:07:18.99,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Laid an ambush for us, did they?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:18.99,0:07:22.93,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,I saw signs that they moved in a hurry. \NThey caught wind of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.00,0:07:27.89,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'll draw their attention. \NYou escape in the meantime.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:29.28,0:07:32.38,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Scarlett, look after Miss Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:32.38,0:07:33.76,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.86,0:07:49.98,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.98,0:07:51.25,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Don't lose your head!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.02,0:07:54.02,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What do you think you can do?!
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.02,0:07:55.79,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,But His Lordship's going to—
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.08,0:07:58.02,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What should I do, Scarlett?!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.34,0:08:04.83,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,This won't be easy.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:05.85,0:08:09.26,Main - Italics,Randolph {M},0,0,0,,Did Miss Grail make it out safely?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.41,0:08:16.10,Main - Italics,Randolph {M},0,0,0,,It's funny.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:16.51,0:08:20.46,Main - Italics,Randolph {M},0,0,0,,Amid all this, I only care \Nabout what happens to her.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:22.36,0:08:23.60,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Should I risk it?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:32.45,0:08:33.87,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Scarlett?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.67,0:08:38.88,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I asked you to look after Miss Grail...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.76,0:08:43.21,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Then again, you would never \Ntake orders from anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:43.21,0:08:44.90,Default,Man G,0,0,0,,I see him! He's over here!
Dialogue: 0,0:08:46.62,0:08:47.96,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You have my thanks.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:57.53,0:09:00.48,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Honestly, you look pathetic.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:00.48,0:09:03.48,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Scarlett! You're not hurt, are you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.74,0:09:07.60,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Of course not. Who do you \Nthink you're talking to?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.05,0:09:09.85,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, thank goodness!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.35,0:09:16.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.32,0:09:19.61,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Are you wounded?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.12,0:09:22.36,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I thought I told you to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.79,0:09:24.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, Your stupid Lordship!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:26.48,0:09:29.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,How could I possibly leave you \Nin that situation and run away?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:29.99,0:09:31.88,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Oh, honestly!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:32.14,0:09:34.38,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You... Your Stupidship!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.38,0:09:35.85,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,"Stupidship"?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.73,0:09:39.95,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That's right! You're\N His stupid Lordship! His Stupidship!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:39.95,0:09:41.52,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Does that bother you?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.46,0:09:48.26,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,What are you laughing for?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:50.19,0:09:51.53,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Why...
Dialogue: 0,0:09:52.20,0:09:53.51,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,are you crying?
Dialogue: 0,0:09:54.92,0:09:56.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Because I was scared!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.78,0:09:58.10,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That's why I told you to escape.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:58.10,0:10:01.87,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No! I was scared because \NI thought you might die!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.87,0:10:03.78,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Can't you get that through your head?!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:03.78,0:10:06.54,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Stupidship! You big, dumb oaf!
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.77,0:10:11.79,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:12.61,0:10:14.00,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,was scared too.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:15.63,0:10:17.61,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Scared I might lose you.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.55,0:10:24.89,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I guess we're alike, Connie.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.93,0:10:31.56,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I-If you think a smile is all it takes to \Nplacate me, you couldn't be more wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:38.90,0:10:40.41,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,If allowed...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:44.18,0:10:45.58,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,If I'm allowed,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.69,0:10:51.19,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I would like to walk \Nthrough life at your side.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:54.95,0:10:55.91,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.88,0:10:58.13,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll allow it.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:59.53,0:11:01.07,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You have my permission.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:02.03,0:11:06.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No matter who else withholds theirs, \Nand even if the gods object,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:07.74,0:11:09.71,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll allow you everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:10.06,0:11:14.44,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So Your Lordship has nothing \Nwhatsoever to worry about.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.13,0:11:20.59,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Should anyone insist on finding fault\N with you in spite of that,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.29,0:11:23.99,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'll slap them good and proper.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:25.48,0:11:27.24,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What man could resist that line?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.99,0:11:33.10,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You say the most outrageous \Nthings sometimes.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.06,0:11:36.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I... I know I need to work on that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:41.29,0:11:42.88,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,Please do.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:50.10,0:11:53.02,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,If you're going to blame someone,\Nblame Abigail.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:54.06,0:11:56.76,Default,Lucia,0,0,0,,Abby's done nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.05,0:12:00.95,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,True. That woman is always in the right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.95,0:12:03.28,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I truly cannot stomach her.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.57,0:12:09.04,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Imagine the look on that hypocrite's face \Nwhen I send her your head.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.14,0:12:14.45,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,Okay, hold it right there.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.45,0:12:15.72,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Salvador?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:16.49,0:12:18.55,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,I'll thank you not to interfere.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.55,0:12:21.17,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,I'd normally be happy to oblige,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:21.48,0:12:24.90,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,but I make it my policy not to kill kids.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:28.53,0:12:30.96,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,So go back to your convent
Dialogue: 0,0:12:32.22,0:12:36.18,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,and keep the Security Force's \Neyes on you.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.75,0:12:40.19,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,Y-You dare to treat me like...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:40.19,0:12:44.48,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,Oh, but we don't want you\N telling any tales.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.48,0:12:47.15,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,I'd prefer to rip out\Nyour tongue, but well...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:51.40,0:12:54.54,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,Work her over so she can't talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:55.45,0:12:59.97,Default,Deborah,0,0,0,,No! No!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:00.81,0:13:03.72,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,Now then, you can run on home.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:04.06,0:13:05.61,Default,Ulysses,0,0,0,,Help...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:12.47,0:13:14.84,Default,Salvador,0,0,0,,You're a sharp one.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:20.74,0:13:23.10,Default,San,0,0,0,,They were even serving him meals.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.09,0:13:26.80,Default,San,0,0,0,,It certainly looks like\Nthey kept Uly alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:27.23,0:13:29.50,Default,San,0,0,0,,Why don't they kill him, though?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:31.05,0:13:37.53,Default,San,0,0,0,,The fact that Uly was abducted in this \Ncountry is all Faris needs to start a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:38.25,0:13:44.37,Default,San,0,0,0,,Theophilis already acts like he's king. \NHis agents would dispose of Uly at once.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:45.25,0:13:51.28,Default,San,0,0,0,,After all, only he and Uly \Ninherited the bluish-violet eyes
Dialogue: 0,0:13:51.28,0:13:53.38,Default,San,0,0,0,,that mark our royalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:53.81,0:13:57.52,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,So if Prince Ulysses is being kept alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.52,0:14:00.89,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,Theophilis isn't the one behind this.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.25,0:14:05.86,Default,Eularia,0,0,0,,And the only contender who hasn't \Nrenounced his right to the throne is...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.42,0:14:11.02,Default,San,0,0,0,,Eularia, we're going to see Kendall.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:11.77,0:14:13.75,Default,San,0,0,0,,Our enemy isn't Theophilis.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:14.99,0:14:17.87,Default,San,0,0,0,,It's Second Prince Roderick.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:20.79,0:14:23.79,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Where could Lucia have gone?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.79,0:14:28.46,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Abigail's people are searching \Nand haven't found a clue.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.81,0:14:33.63,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,And Deborah turned up \Nin no condition to talk.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:34.29,0:14:36.20,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,What on earth is going on?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.84,0:14:38.89,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Constance Grail?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.91,0:14:43.64,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,It's been too long.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.15,0:14:45.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Pamela...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:45.89,0:14:49.71,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,You haven't changed a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.71,0:14:53.66,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,What about me? Don't I seem \Na little different to you?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.42,0:15:00.44,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,To tell the truth,\N I spotted you not long ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:00.44,0:15:03.42,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,In a warehouse on the Grafton wharf.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:03.42,0:15:06.42,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I th-think you must be mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.42,0:15:07.61,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Do you now?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.67,0:15:11.92,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Well, it doesn't really matter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:16.95,0:15:19.94,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,King Ernst is going to Melvina?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:20.58,0:15:27.43,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,The grenades at the wharf were made\Nwith smuggled explosives from Melvina.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:27.89,0:15:32.69,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,In exchange for overlooking that fact, \Nhe wants a trade agreement on arms
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.03,0:15:35.47,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,that will act as a check against Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.49,0:15:38.67,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Explosives from Melvina...?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.24,0:15:41.70,Default,Scared,0,0,0,,Lily mentioned that in her letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.02,0:15:46.50,Flashback,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I'm having explosives \Nsmuggled in from Melvina.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:47.09,0:15:49.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Crown Princess Cecilia!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:52.57,0:15:54.55,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,What's the meaning of this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:54.91,0:15:59.31,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,You never breathed a word \Nof a pact with Melvina to me!
Dialogue: 0,0:15:59.31,0:16:01.24,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,A strange reaction.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.24,0:16:04.53,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Melvina borders the Luze domain \Nwhere you grew up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:04.53,0:16:08.21,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,And all the agreement will do is \Nlet us trade freely with them.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.12,0:16:11.29,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,So, why are you so flustered?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.41,0:16:16.32,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,I've waited a long time for this day,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.98,0:16:21.87,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,when the explosives you smuggled in \Nsaw use on our soil.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.54,0:16:25.14,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,How long have you known?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.08,0:16:30.31,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Why do you think I married you \Ndespite objections from all sides?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:30.96,0:16:35.08,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Why do you think my father \Nand Duke Castiel gave their blessings?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.99,0:16:37.38,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,From the very beginning?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:39.97,0:16:45.85,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Is this wise? You could be \Naccused yourself if word gets out.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.92,0:16:48.37,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,Didn't you know?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:52.29,0:16:56.31,Default,Enrique,0,0,0,,I've been guilty for a long time now.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:01.38,0:17:04.33,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,I always knew you were careless.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:09.59,0:17:13.06,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,Come quickly! Enrique's having a fit!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.47,0:17:19.29,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,You didn't kill him?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.86,0:17:24.10,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,He is still a prince. It's easier \Nfor me to act with him alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:25.87,0:17:27.35,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.79,0:17:30.68,Default,Cecilia,0,0,0,,They've already moved Ulysses \Nto that dungeon.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:31.10,0:17:33.61,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Now everything is in place.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:34.33,0:17:37.01,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Yes, there have been many \Nunforeseen developments,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:38.08,0:17:40.12,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,but now is our time to strike.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.35,0:17:43.37,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Oh, but first...
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.84,0:17:50.26,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,we must dispose of nuisances.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.04,0:17:58.43,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Really, it was only by chance!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.23,0:18:01.55,Default,Reporter,0,0,0,,Extra! Extra!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:01.81,0:18:03.80,Default,Commoner A,0,0,0,,A prince was kidnapped?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.80,0:18:06.90,Default,Commoner B,0,0,0,,They say Faris is ready to go to war!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:07.61,0:18:12.79,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I went to the Grafton domain \Non my physician's advice.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:12.79,0:18:14.32,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,And there, I just so happened
Dialogue: 0,0:18:14.68,0:18:19.33,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,to witness a friend of mine \Nshove a sobbing child into a carriage.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:19.33,0:18:22.06,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,I couldn't put it out of my mind,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:22.06,0:18:24.58,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,so I asked her about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:24.58,0:18:28.82,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,But she panicked and told me\N I had to be mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.43,0:18:30.59,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,Looking back, I realize...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.59,0:18:33.44,Default,Pamela,0,0,0,,that must have been Prince Ulysses.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:35.03,0:18:36.75,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, that's their game.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.75,0:18:39.10,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,Constance Grail, I believe?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:39.60,0:18:44.84,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,I hereby arrest you for aiding and \Nabetting the abduction of Ulysses Faris.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:47.23,0:18:49.34,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I've done nothing wrong.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.74,0:18:52.85,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,Did Randolph Ulster do the dirty work?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.95,0:18:59.11,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,We have testimony\N that Ulster drew his gun.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:00.40,0:19:02.37,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,So that's how it's going to be.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:02.73,0:19:06.40,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Someone must be questioning \NHis Lordship as we speak.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.40,0:19:12.09,Main - Italics,Connie {M},0,0,0,,Time wasted on us delays the search for \NPrince Ulysses and moves us closer to war.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:15.32,0:19:16.64,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.64,0:19:21.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,No. I was a party to the abduction \Nof Prince Ulysses.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:23.18,0:19:24.89,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I had backers.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:25.45,0:19:30.01,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Ruthless criminals who don't hesitate \Nto kill to get what they want.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:30.01,0:19:31.52,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,You wouldn't!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.88,0:19:33.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,The name of their organization...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:33.27,0:19:34.52,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,Hey, wait!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.37,0:19:36.77,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,is Daeg Gallus.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:38.29,0:19:40.03,Default,Scarlett,0,0,0,,Connie, you idiot!
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.38,0:19:42.18,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Did you get all that?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:43.41,0:19:45.15,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I have more to confess.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:45.47,0:19:47.85,Default,Gaina,0,0,0,,Stop. That's enough.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.15,0:19:49.29,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,In that case,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:50.55,0:19:52.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,please summon Viscount Hamsworth.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.84,0:19:56.65,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,My engagement to Earl Randolph Ulster...
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.05,0:19:59.68,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,must be broken off.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.30,0:20:05.92,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,Your Lordship! So they let you go.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:07.09,0:20:09.18,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,What are you thinking?!
Dialogue: 0,0:20:09.18,0:20:14.40,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,You won't be free to act \Nunless we sever all ties.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.43,0:20:19.51,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,You're going to cast me off?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:24.54,0:20:29.95,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,If the day comes when this is all over \Nand we can laugh together again,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:29.95,0:20:32.27,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,I'd like to drop in on \Na certain someone uninvited.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:34.20,0:20:40.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,That someone is strong and kind \Nand always in the right,
Dialogue: 0,0:20:40.57,0:20:46.82,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,but he's such an oaf that he's convinced \Nhimself he can't make anyone happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:48.24,0:20:52.81,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,So, this time, I want to be \Nthe one to take him by the hand.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:54.89,0:20:56.99,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,That will prove difficult.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:58.98,0:21:01.92,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'm certain you'll be proposed to first...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:03.12,0:21:09.71,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,by a dull man who can't manage a witty \Nremark or pick a decent spot for a date.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.68,0:21:28.04,Default,Connie,0,0,0,,On my forehead?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:28.93,0:21:31.89,Default,Randolph,0,0,0,,I'm not engaged to you at the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.08,0:21:38.90,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Your Royal Highness Prince Johan,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:44.19,0:21:47.65,Signs,Signs,0,0,0,,SECOND PRINCE JOHAN ADELBIDE
Dialogue: 0,0:21:40.23,0:21:42.76,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,have you reached a decision?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:43.14,0:21:47.40,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,How many times must I tell you?\N I'm only standing in for the king.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:51.22,0:21:53.16,Default,Johan,0,0,0,,Villain! This is my daughter's!
Dialogue: 0,0:21:53.40,0:21:58.41,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Have no fear. Your precious daughter \Nhas not suffered a scratch...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.05,0:22:01.42,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,for the moment.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.96,0:22:06.13,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,Faris desires war.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:06.13,0:22:08.80,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,To convince them to\N stay their raised fist,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.80,0:22:11.46,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,you must make an example
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.05,0:22:14.12,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,by publicly executing...
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.73,0:22:18.31,Default,Rufus,0,0,0,,the kidnapper, Constance Grail.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.68,0:22:33.68,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(480,524)\fs10\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(160.923,245.743)}Translation:\N{\fs12}William Varteresian
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.89,0:22:38.89,Default,Credits,0,0,0,,{\an8\fad(500,520)\fs10\fnArial\c&H351F51&\3c&H9985A7&\blur1\shad0\pos(158.769,266.077)}Subtitle Timing:\N{\fs12}Edgar Cruz\N\N\N{\fs10}Subtitle Editing:\N{\fs12}Riley Dalton
